From: MGS2 RG353VS compatibility port
Subject: [PATCH] libdg: store the requested value in DG_NopRenderState

DG_NopRenderState is meant to update libdg's render-state shadow without
issuing a D3D8 call. Both the inline production body and the out-of-line body
instead store the state enum, ignoring their Value argument. A later
DG_SetRenderState(State, State) can then be skipped even though that value was
never established.

Store Value in both definitions. The recovered source and map contain no
DG_NopRenderState caller, so this is a source-only audit correction and not a
runtime or flicker candidate. The distributed game executable is not stored or
modified by this record.

--- a/mgs2x/source/system/libdg/wd3d.c
+++ b/mgs2x/source/system/libdg/wd3d.c
@@ -932,7 +932,7 @@
 
 void DG_NopRenderState(D3DRENDERSTATETYPE State, DWORD Value)
 {
-	DG_RenderStateValue[State] = State ;	// 状態だけ設定
+	DG_RenderStateValue[State] = Value ;	// 状態だけ設定
 }
 
 #endif
--- a/mgs2x/source/system/libdg/libdgw.h
+++ b/mgs2x/source/system/libdg/libdgw.h
@@ -2152,7 +2152,7 @@
 
 inline void DG_NopRenderState(D3DRENDERSTATETYPE State, DWORD Value)
 {
-	DG_RenderStateValue[State] = State ;
+	DG_RenderStateValue[State] = Value ;
 }
 
 #endif
